<decision #mission.restore_property_first_orm_modeling.authority { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "low; restoring detached relation authoring would recreate competing schema authorities" } (
  <question ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCJ>
  关联关系的建模 authority 应位于 field、独立 relation 原语，还是 class navigation property？
  </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCJ>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCK>
    必须位于 Order.shop、Shop.orders、Department.employees 这类 property，不能位于 shopId 等 field，也不能由独立 relation 原语拥有。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCK>
    <decision-text ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCM>
    Kunun typed navigation property 及其 ORM metadata 是关系声明的唯一 authoring authority；field 只参与存储映射，compiled relation graph 只是派生投影。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCM>
    <rationale ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCN>
    property-first 符合 class/code-first 语义，并使多字段关联不受单一外键 field 限制；独立 relation 原语会与对象属性形成双真源。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCN>
    <evidence ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCP>
    用户明确重申历史约束；当前 depa ORM 文档、compiler 和 composer 反向使用 relationships/relation 节点，构成已证实的实现漂移。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCP>
  )>
)>

<decision #mission.restore_property_first_orm_modeling.code_first_authority { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "low" } (
  <question ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCQ>
  depa ORM code-first API 应拥有独立的 entity/relation builder，还是复用 Kunun 类型系统？
  </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCQ>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCR>
    强烈要求引用 Kunun 类型系统进行 code-first API 的 DSL 建模。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCR>
    <decision-text ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCS>
    Kunun public type-system model owns code-first class/field/property construction；depa ORM 仅提供 metadata/profile adapter 和编译投影，不维护 shadow RelationModel authority。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCS>
    <rationale ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCT>
    source-first 与 code-first 必须在同一类型系统模型上收敛，才能避免 parser、builder 和 runtime 各自演化出不同 schema。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCT>
    <evidence ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCV>
    用户明确约束；当前 depa ORM CodeFirstOrmSourceComposer 自有 EntityModel/RelationModel 并输出 relationships section。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCV>
  )>
)>

<decision #mission.restore_property_first_orm_modeling.composite_and_inverse { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "medium; metadata vocabulary may evolve while single ownership remains fixed" } (
  <question ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCW>
  复合字段关联和双向 navigation property 如何避免重复 authority？
  </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCW>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCX>
    relation 不能建立在 field 上，因为后续多字段关联会受限并形成技术债。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCX>
    <decision-text ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCY>
    owning navigation property 持有有序 local/target field tuples 和物理关系 metadata；inverse navigation property 仅以稳定 property identity 引用 owner，不重复 storage mapping。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCY>
    <rationale ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCZ>
    有序 tuple 支持多字段关联；owner/inverse 分工让两个真实业务 property 共存而不产生两份可写 join 真值。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHCZ>
    <evidence ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD0>
    用户对多字段技术债的明确说明；现有 OrmRelationSchema 已能表达 endpoint key arrays，可作为派生 runtime contract。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD0>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.migrate_orm_consumers_to_named_conf.dependency_provenance { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "medium" } (
  <question ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD1>
  未发布的 Kunun 1.0.4 与 depa ORM 0.2.0 如何证明正式 package boundary，而不把本地路径写入仓库？
  </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD1>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD2>
    提交态只使用正式 semver；验证态使用带版本和 SHA-256 的临时 sibling tarball，并在隔离目录安装。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD2>
    <decision-text ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD3>
    capsule 和 kon-spl-dsl manifests 声明正式版本；临时 tarball 不进入提交依赖或 lock authority；isolated consumer 必须证明 resolution 不经过 sibling/global/workspace symlink。ignored bun.lock 保持未被 Git 管理、只报告 stale versions 且不得参与 proof；registry-only authoritative lock 延后至 mission G5。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD3>
    <rationale ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD4>
    同时保留未来 npm consumption 的真实声明和当前未发布条件下可复现的 package-boundary 证据。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD4>
    <evidence ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD5>
    plan-track fresh observer 发现 manifests/ignored lock 为旧版本而 installed modules 是全局软链，目标 registry versions 当前不可用。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD5>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.migrate_orm_consumers_to_named_conf.generator_retirement { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "low" } (
  <question ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD6>
  既有 property migration generator 在此次 hard cut 后应如何处理？
  </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD6>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD7>
    先用完整 oracle 做一次性 canonical migration，再物理删除或封闭 legacy reader/emitter。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD7>
    <decision-text ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD8>
    迁移工具必须先改为输出 NamedConf、flat Field 和 declaration-owned datasource identity；完成 30/82/216 semantic comparison 后，不保留可重新生成旧契约的兼容入口。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD8>
    <rationale ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD9>
    长期保留 legacy reader 会让旧契约继续成为事实上的输入语言，与用户要求的无兼容改造冲突。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHD9>
    <evidence ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDA>
    fresh observer 定位 migrate-property-relation-fixtures.ts 仍输出旧 marker 并重建 nested storage。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDA>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.migrate_orm_consumers_to_named_conf.negative_classification { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "low" } (
  <question ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDB>
  哪些旧语法 literal 可以在 hard cut 后保留？
  </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDB>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDC>
    仅 immutable archive 与直接断言旧输入被拒绝的最小 negative literal。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDC>
    <decision-text ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDD>
    文件名含 invalid、break 或 conflict 不自动豁免；正向 runtime 场景中的模型必须 canonical。active Codument evidence 必须分类并报告，不能通过排除 codument/** 隐藏。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDD>
    <rationale ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDE>
    豁免由行为目的决定，而不是由目录或命名猜测，才能防止兼容输入悄悄回流。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDE>
    <evidence ?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDF>
    fresh observer 发现 direct datasource 用例实际断言无关 network environment error，而不是旧输入 rejection。
    </?01KZVEK9J38PE4N9FHMDX1SHDF>
  )>
)>

<decision #mission.canonicalize_orm_annotation_named_conf.transport {
  priority = "P0"
  status = "accepted"
  durable_candidate = true
  confidence = "high"
  reversibility = "low; accepting two transports would recreate competing annotation authorities"
}
(
  <question ?>ORM profile kind and payload should be represented by marker name plus Conf, target-internal configuration, or KnKnot.NamedConf on a prefix annotation?</?>
  <answer { }
  (
    <raw-answer ?>ORM must remain an annotation attached to class, field, prop, or datasource, and these profiles must use KnKnot.NamedConf.</?>
    <decision-text ?>Use prefix annotations with one NamedConf profile: `:entity` on class, `:field` on Field, `:relation` on typed Property, and `:datasource` on datasource declaration. NamedConf is transport only; the Kunun public type-system model remains semantic authority.</?>
    <rationale ?>The mapping uses the language's native named-configuration capability without embedding ORM configuration inside modeled declarations or creating a second type model.</?>
    <evidence ?>User corrected the target-internal proposal and explicitly confirmed the prefix-annotation NamedConf design.</?>
  )>
)>

<decision #mission.canonicalize_orm_annotation_named_conf.property_authority {
  priority = "P0"
  status = "accepted"
  durable_candidate = true
  confidence = "high"
  reversibility = "low"
}
(
  <question ?>After changing annotation transport, where does relationship semantic and physical mapping authority remain?</?>
  <answer { }
  (
    <raw-answer ?>Relationships must be modeled on properties such as Order.shop and Shop.orders, never on foreign-key fields or a detached relation primitive.</?>
    <decision-text ?>Typed Kunun navigation Property remains the sole relation authority. The owner Property owns ordered join tuples, through topology, physical join mapping, and write policy; an inverse Property only references the stable owner Property identity.</?>
    <rationale ?>This preserves the completed property-first mission and supports composite joins without coupling a relationship to one foreign-key Field.</?>
    <evidence ?>Explicit user constraint and the archived property-first durable decisions.</?>
  )>
)>

<decision #mission.canonicalize_orm_annotation_named_conf.field_shape {
  priority = "P0"
  status = "accepted"
  durable_candidate = true
  confidence = "high"
  reversibility = "medium"
}
(
  <question ?>Should the Field ORM profile retain a nested `storage` object and may it contain relationship storage information?</?>
  <answer { }
  (
    <raw-answer ?>Remove the storage nesting, but do not leave any relationship definition on a Field.</?>
    <decision-text ?>The `:field` NamedConf and `OrmKununMetadata.field(...)` use one flat profile limited to scalar/column persistence, index, and validation. Relation role, tuples, through topology, inverse, and write authority are invalid on Fields.</?>
    <rationale ?>Flattening removes unnecessary transport nesting while a strict allowlist prevents the earlier field-owned relation drift from returning under a new shape.</?>
    <evidence ?>User explicitly requested removal of `storage` and zero residual field relation configuration.</?>
  )>
)>

<decision #mission.canonicalize_orm_annotation_named_conf.datasource_authority {
  priority = "P0"
  status = "accepted"
  durable_candidate = true
  confidence = "high"
  reversibility = "low"
}
(
  <question ?>How should `(datasource #main)` and `orm :datasource` divide responsibility?</?>
  <answer { }
  (
    <raw-answer ?>Use `#(orm :datasource={ kind, env_conn, options })(datasource #main)` as the canonical model.</?>
    <decision-text ?>The datasource declaration name is the sole identity/reference authority. The `:datasource` NamedConf is the sole ORM provider, environment connection, and options authority. Annotation `key`/`name`, direct datasource Conf, missing ORM configuration, and fallback projection are rejected.</?>
    <rationale ?>The declaration and annotation remain complementary while eliminating the current annotation-versus-direct-Conf dual path and duplicated identity.</?>
    <evidence ?>User explicitly accepted the recommended datasource form and hard-cut semantics.</?>
  )>
)>

<decision #mission.canonicalize_orm_annotation_named_conf.compatibility {
  priority = "P0"
  status = "accepted"
  durable_candidate = true
  confidence = "high"
  reversibility = "low"
}
(
  <question ?>Should production readers retain old syntax compatibility during migration?</?>
  <answer { }
  (
    <raw-answer ?>This must be a complete migration with no compatibility residue.</?>
    <decision-text ?>Remove old readers, fallbacks, and dual emitters. Live source, positive fixtures, current docs, app bundles, generated artifacts, and package tarballs must contain zero accepted old syntax; only explicit negative tests and immutable Codument archives are exempt.</?>
    <rationale ?>A controlled three-project migration can move atomically, while compatibility would preserve exactly the authority drift this mission is intended to remove.</?>
    <evidence ?>User confirmed the recommended no-compatibility scope and requested a residue scan including web IDE application bundles.</?>
  )>
)>
